   "rule": {
    "title": "Six endings, one pattern",
    "body": "Take the dictionary form, drop -ω, add: -ω -εις -ει -ομεν -ετε -ουσι(ν). λέγει = he says, λέγομεν = we say. The present describes what is happening or what happens in general. δεῖ (from δέω) is a fixed third-person form: 'it is necessary'.",
    "examples": [
     {
      "gr": "πιστεύομεν",
      "en": "we believe"
     },
     {
      "gr": "τί λέγεις;",
      "en": "what do you say?"
     },
     {
      "gr": "δεῖ ὑμᾶς γεννηθῆναι ἄνωθεν",
      "en": "you must be born from above"
     }
    ]
   },
