   "rule": {
    "title": "Augment = past",
    "body": "A past tense in the indicative is marked at the FRONT of the verb by an augment: ἐ- before a consonant (λύω → ἔλυον), or a lengthened vowel (ἀκούω → ἤκουον, ἔχω → εἶχον). The imperfect is the past of the present: ongoing or repeated action, 'was doing', 'used to do'. ἦν (was) is the imperfect of εἰμί.",
    "examples": [
     {
      "gr": "ἔλεγεν αὐτοῖς",
      "en": "he was saying to them / he used to tell them"
