   "rule": {
    "title": "The verb as a noun",
    "body": "-ειν (active) and -εσθαι (middle/passive) make an infinitive: λύειν 'to loose', ἔρχεσθαι 'to come'. It completes verbs like θέλω, δύναμαι, μέλλω, δεῖ, and with the article it works as a noun (τὸ ζῆν, living). The subject of an infinitive goes in the accusative.",
